{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And took me</b> — I was compelled. And he further explained another interpretation: because he said to him, \"there eat bread,\" he said to him: I am not like the false prophets who prophesy for bread, nor a son of a false prophet, for I have no need for bread, for <b>I am a tender of sycamore figs</b>." "And the word <b>bôles</b> — it has no cognate, and in the Ishmaelite tongue it is like one who dries, and <b>šiqmîm</b> [sycamores] is a fruit resembling figs, and it is not found in these lands; and in the Ishmaelite tongue gamîn, also šiqem. And behold, I did not prophesy out of need, so how could I abandon the words of HaShem who commanded me to prophesy, and obey you who say, 'Do not prophesy'?!"], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:32.141079911Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}